    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d850">

                <pb facs="0815" n="809" xml:id="pg809"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.48 Refugees/1929: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Jerusalem</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Steger</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Jerusalem</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-10-23T13:00:00+02:00">October 23, 1939—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 23—11:29 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>12. Immigration schedule for the period October 1, 1939 to March 31, 1940
                    published in <hi rendition="#italic">Official Gazette</hi> on October 19,
                    provides for issuance during that time of 300 certificates for non-Jews plus
                    certificates as may be required for their dependents. As reported in Consulate
                    General’s despatch 1018 of July 21, Jewish immigration for the period was
                    suspended and no certificates for Jews were authorized.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Steger</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
